      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) that makes the four-digit number \\( 712n \\) divisible by 18, we need to ensure that the number is both divisible by 2 and by 9. A number is divisible by 2 if its units digit is even, and a number is divisible by 9 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 9.\n\n1. **Check divisibility by 2:**\n   The units digit \\( n \\) must be even for the number to be divisible by 2. The possible values for \\( n \\) are 0, 2, 4, 6, and 8.\n\n2. **Check the sum of the digits:**\n   The sum of the digits of \\( 712n \\) is \\( 7 + 1 + 2 + n = 10 + n \\). For the number to be divisible by 9, \\( 10 + n \\) must be divisible by 9. We need to find which of the even values for \\( n \\) make \\( 10 + n \\) divisible by 9.\n   \n   - If \\( n = 0 \\), then \\( 10 + 0 = 10 \\) (not divisible by 9).\n   - If \\( n = 2 \\), then \\( 10 + 2 = 12 \\) (not divisible by 9).\n   - If \\( n = 4 \\), then \\( 10 + 4 = 14 \\) (not divisible by 9).\n   - If \\( n = 6 \\), then \\( 10 + 6 = 16 \\) (not divisible by 9).\n   - If \\( n = 8 \\), then \\( 10 + 8 = 18 \\) (divisible by 9 because \\( 18 \\div 9 = 2 \\)).\n\n   So, \\( n = 8 \\) is the only value that satisfies both conditions.\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( n \\) is \\( \\boxed{8} \\).",
